	)
	(text "5 V INPUT CURRENT BUDGET - SINGLE BOARD AND SIX-BOARD CHAIN\n\n1. BASE LOAD PER BOARD - RGB ARRAY IN SHUTDOWN\n\nU1 RP2040: Use I_MCU for the total current drawn from +3V3 by U1.\nInclude VREG_VIN, IOVDD, USB_VDD, and ADC_AVDD. Count the core\nload through VREG_VIN once. The project operating value is pending\nfirmware configuration and measurement. See RP2040 datasheet §5.7.2.\n\nOther ICs - selected reference values for this calculation:\nU2 W25Q16JV: 25 mA max. during program/erase. At 50 MHz,\n    read current is 4 mA typ. / 15 mA max. (Winbond Rev. I, §10.4).\nU3 TCA9534: 0.030 mA max. at 3.6 V, 400 kHz, inputs, no load.\nU4 TMAG5273: 3.0 mA in low-noise conversion, or 2.3 mA\n    in low-power conversion. Use 3.0 mA for this calculation.\nU5 LM75A: 1.0 mA max. in normal mode with I²C active.\n    With I²C inactive, normal-mode current is 0.10 mA typ.\nU6 VEML3328: 1.0 mA max. supply current.\nU7 ICM-42605: 0.65 mA typ. in six-axis low-noise mode\n    at VDD = VDDIO = 1.8 V. Verify at the board's 3.3 V.\nU8 AP2112K-3.3: 0.080 mA max. quiescent current at 4.3 V, no load.\nU9/U10 LM66100: Allow 0.0006 mA for both ICs using the\n    0.30 µA/device enabled no-load reference at 3.6 V.\nU11 IS31FL3254: 0.0018 mA max. in shutdown at 5 V.\nSubtotal excluding U1 and external loads: approximately 30.8 mA.\nThis subtotal combines specified maxima and condition-specific\nreference values.\n\n2. EXTERNAL LOADS - NOMINAL RAILS AND RESISTOR VALUES\n\nSix I²C links, 12 × 2.2 kΩ pull-ups:\n    3.3 V / 2.2 kΩ = 1.50 mA per low line.\n    All 12 lines low simultaneously: 18.0 mA. For expected\n    operation, multiply each line's current by its low duty cycle.\nRN1 DIP pull-ups: 8 × 3.3 V / 10 kΩ = 2.64 mA, all switches closed.\nR10/R11 user buttons: 2 × 3.3 V / 10 kΩ = 0.66 mA, both pressed.\nD1-D3 and D12: four 1 kΩ series resistors. For each lit LED,\n    I ≈ (Vdrive − VF) / 1 kΩ. Allow up to 3.30 mA per branch\n    at nominal 3.3 V using the resistor-only bound (VF = 0).\n    Allow 13.20 mA total. Actual LED current is lower.\nR1 RUN: 0.33 mA with RESET held.\nR2/R3 BOOTSEL: approximately 0.30 mA through the divider\n    with BOOTSEL held and QSPI_SS undriven.\nR17 Hall INT pull-up: 0.33 mA if the output pulls low.\nR23/R24 power select: allow 1.00 mA total using 5 V / 10 kΩ\n    per branch as a resistor-only bound.\nR29 LED_SDB pull-down: up to 0.033 mA while driven high.\nExternal-load allowance: approximately 36.5 mA per board.\nThis deliberately combines simultaneous low, pressed, and lit\nconditions for budgeting. Normal average load depends on activity.\n\n3. ADDITIONAL LOAD - ONE RGB ARRAY ACTIVE\n\nR28 = 15 kΩ. Nominal full-white channel load:\n    8 RGB LEDs × 3 channels × 5.06 mA ≈ 121.4 mA.\nU11 active overhead reference: 3.4 mA typ. / 4.1 mA max.\n    at VCC = 5 V and RISET = 3.3 kΩ under datasheet test settings.\nNominal full-white load plus typical overhead reference ≈ 125 mA.\nVerify driver overhead, channel current tolerance, PWM settings,\nand full-white current with the board's 15 kΩ ISET resistor.\n\n4. 5 V INPUT - PRELIMINARY CALCULATION\n\nUsing the reference values and external-load allowance above:\nSingle board, RGB off ≈ I_MCU + 67.3 mA.\nSingle board, RGB full white ≈ I_MCU + 192 mA.\nSix boards from one 5 V source, one RGB array full white:\n    ≈ 6 × I_MCU + 529 mA, assuming the same MCU allowance per board.\nFor different MCU loads, sum the six MCU currents individually.\nThese are reference calculations. Final expected current and\nworst-case design limits are pending the checks below.\n\n5. FIRMWARE AND HARDWARE INPUTS TO CONFIRM\n\nFirmware: RP2040 system clock, workload on each core, USB activity,\nQSPI clock and read/write/erase activity, sensor modes and sample\nrates, I²C line activity, and user LED/RGB PWM and current settings.\nConfirm shutdown of inactive arrays and enforce at most one active\narray across the chain, including startup and reset.\n\nHardware: Confirm the 5 V source capability, cable and connector\nvoltage drop, startup inrush, protection thresholds, and thermal\nmargin. Measure single-board and six-board input current with\nthe intended firmware before finalizing the protection ratings."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
